 # fc_nnue_h256_e12_ep12_ep10base — H256 net (run e, epoch 12) on the locked ep10 source base
+
+## Sol exact int32 AVX2 research option — 20261025
+
+The independent `FORGE_NNUE_EXACT_INT32_AVX2` CMake option defaults OFF. Build with it ON and the existing H256/strict FP flags, then set `NnueExactInt32` true before the first go or bench. The runtime option also defaults OFF. Activation is acknowledged once after actual int32 work; bench counters distinguish backend execution.
+
+The ON path widens stored weights into int32 accumulators and converts the exact 1/4096 grid into the unchanged float output calculation. It never requantizes output. Feature-enabled builds add2048 bytes per H256 accumulator even with the runtime option OFF. No speed or Elo claim; adoption requires independent box/Windows evidence. Idea sources: user Job A fixed-grid review and Intel AVX2 semantics; original code and tests only.
 
 Status: **UNPROVEN. No Elo or strength claim.** Built on the box by Engine Coder, 2026-10-23.
 
